IMPORT `roc-core`
IMPORT `roc-definitions`

-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore), G.N. No. S 914/2021, current version as at 5 November 2026.
-- ORDERS 29 AND 29A: REFERRALS ON ISSUES OF LAW; REQUESTS FOR OPINIONS ON QUESTIONS OF FOREIGN LAW.  LAYER 1.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from Singapore Statutes Online.
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here has been checked against the official text.
-- Written with a macro builder that quotes the source lines and writes the @ref; the builder is not part of this row, so edit this file directly.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT.  Every decision function answers `MAYBE BOOLEAN`.
--   JUST TRUE    the Rule says yes on these facts.
--   JUST FALSE   the Rule says no in its own words: a "means" definition, a flat negative, an "if" or "where" condition unmet.
--   NOTHING      the Rule does not answer: a power limited by its own wording, a list that is not closed, a silence.
-- Both Orders define "Court" for themselves as the General Division, the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal
-- (O 29 r 1, O 29A r 1); the functions below use that meaning through `o 29 r 1 a court is the Court`.

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 29 -- Referrals on issues of law`
-- ===========================================================================

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 1 -- definitions of this Order`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:4408 | 1. In this Order, unless the context otherwise requires — “Court” means the General Division, the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal;
@ref O 29 r 1 (opening words) (src:4408)
GIVEN `the context otherwise requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 29 r 1 a defined term has its defined meaning` MEANS
    IF NOT `the context otherwise requires`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In this Order, unless the context otherwise requires"

-- “Court” means the General Division, the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal (the core's `Court level` names them).
@ref O 29 r 1 “Court” (src:4408)
GIVEN level IS A `Court level`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 29 r 1 a court is the Court` MEANS
    CONSIDER level
    WHEN `General Division` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Appellate Division` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Court of Appeal` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“Court” means the General Division, the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal"

-- src:4409 | “foreign country” means a country or territory outside Singapore;
@ref O 29 r 1 “foreign country” (src:4409)
GIVEN `the place is a country or territory` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the place is outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 29 r 1 a place is a foreign country` MEANS
    IF `the place is a country or territory` AND `the place is outside Singapore`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“foreign country” means a country or territory outside Singapore"

-- The two lists the definitions hand to.  Rule 6: the specified foreign countries.  Rule 7: the specified courts.
DECLARE `o 29 r 6 foreign country` IS ONE OF
    `o 29 r 6(a) New South Wales, Australia`
    `o 29 r 6(b) Dubai, United Arab Emirates`
    `o 29 r 6(c) Bermuda`
    `o 29 r 6 any other foreign country`

DECLARE `o 29 r 7 court` IS ONE OF
    `o 29 r 7(a) a court of competent jurisdiction in New South Wales, Australia`
    `o 29 r 7(b) a court of competent jurisdiction which forms part of the Dubai International Financial Centre Courts`
    `o 29 r 7(c) the Supreme Court of Bermuda`
    `o 29 r 7 any other court`

-- src:4436 | 6. For the purposes of this Order, each of the following is a specified foreign country: ( a )
-- src:4437 | New South Wales, Australia;
-- src:4438 | ( b )
-- src:4439 | Dubai, United Arab Emirates;
-- src:4440 | ( c )
-- src:4441 | Bermuda.
@ref O 29 r 6 (src:4436-4441)
GIVEN country IS A `o 29 r 6 foreign country`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 29 r 6 a place is a specified foreign country` MEANS
    CONSIDER country
    WHEN `o 29 r 6 any other foreign country` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a foreign country that is specified in Rule 6" (Rule 1 hands "specified foreign country" to this list, so a country not on it is not one) (open convention question QC)
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:4443 | 7. For the purposes of this Order — ( a )
-- src:4444 | where the specified foreign country is New South Wales, Australia, every court of competent jurisdiction in New South Wales, Australia is a specified court;
-- src:4445 | ( b )
-- src:4446 | where the specified foreign country is Dubai, United Arab Emirates, every court of competent jurisdiction which forms part of the Dubai International Financial Centre Courts is a specified court; and
-- src:4447 | ( c )
-- src:4448 | where the specified foreign country is Bermuda, the Supreme Court of Bermuda is a specified court.
@ref O 29 r 7 (src:4443-4448)
GIVEN country IS A `o 29 r 6 foreign country`
      court IS A `o 29 r 7 court`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 29 r 7 a court is a specified court` MEANS
    CONSIDER court
    WHEN `o 29 r 7(a) a court of competent jurisdiction in New South Wales, Australia` THEN
        IF country EQUALS `o 29 r 6(a) New South Wales, Australia` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the specified foreign country is New South Wales, Australia": the court is specified under paragraph (a) only where that is the specified foreign country
    WHEN `o 29 r 7(b) a court of competent jurisdiction which forms part of the Dubai International Financial Centre Courts` THEN
        IF country EQUALS `o 29 r 6(b) Dubai, United Arab Emirates` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the specified foreign country is Dubai, United Arab Emirates": the court is specified under paragraph (b) only where that is the specified foreign country
    WHEN `o 29 r 7(c) the Supreme Court of Bermuda` THEN
        IF country EQUALS `o 29 r 6(c) Bermuda` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the specified foreign country is Bermuda": the court is specified under paragraph (c) only where that is the specified foreign country
    WHEN `o 29 r 7 any other court` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a court that is specified in Rule 7" (Rule 1 hands "specified court" to this list, so a court not on it is not one) (open convention question QC)

-- “specified court” means a court that is specified in Rule 7; “specified foreign country” means a foreign country
-- specified in Rule 6.  The definitions hand their meaning to the lists: when no entry holds, the answer is JUST FALSE
-- (ruling of 2026-11-05 (a)).
-- src:4410 | “specified court” means a court that is specified in Rule 7;
@ref O 29 r 1 “specified court” (src:4410)
GIVEN country IS A `o 29 r 6 foreign country`
      court IS A `o 29 r 7 court`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 29 r 1 a court is a specified court` MEANS
    IF `o 29 r 7 a court is a specified court` country court EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“specified court” means a court that is specified in Rule 7"

-- src:4411 | “specified foreign country” means a foreign country that is specified in Rule 6.
@ref O 29 r 1 “specified foreign country” (src:4411)
GIVEN country IS A `o 29 r 6 foreign country`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 29 r 1 a place is a specified foreign country` MEANS
    IF `o 29 r 6 a place is a specified foreign country` country EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“specified foreign country” means a foreign country that is specified in Rule 6"

