-- src:4427 | 5. —(1) Proceedings for the determination of any issue relating to Singapore law which is relevant to an issue in any proceedings before a specified court in a specified foreign country may be commenced by originating application and supported by affidavit. (2) The originating application or supporting affidavit must — ( a )
@ref O 29 r 5(1) (src:4427)
GIVEN `the issue relates to Singapore law and is relevant to an issue in proceedings before a specified court in a specified foreign country` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings are commenced by originating application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is supported by affidavit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 29 r 5(1) proceedings on an issue of Singapore law may be commenced by originating application` MEANS
    IF `the issue relates to Singapore law and is relevant to an issue in proceedings before a specified court in a specified foreign country`
    THEN IF `the proceedings are commenced by originating application` AND `the application is supported by affidavit`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Proceedings for the determination of any issue relating to Singapore law which is relevant to an issue in any proceedings before a specified court in a specified foreign country may be commenced by originating application and supported by affidavit"
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Proceedings for the determination of any issue relating to Singapore law which is relevant to an issue in any proceedings before a specified court in a specified foreign country may be commenced by originating application and supported by affidavit"
