-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `O 29A Rules 2 and 3 -- the request for an opinion`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:4457 | 2. —(1) Where in any proceedings before the Court there arises any question relating to the law of any specified foreign country or to the application of such law, the Court may, on the application of one or more of the parties or on the Court’s own motion, transmit to a specified court in that specified foreign country a request for an opinion on that question (called in this Rule the initial request), and any subsequent request for a clarification that is relevant to the opinion (called in this Rule a subsequent request), if all of the parties consent — ( a )
-- src:4458 | to the transmission of the initial request and any subsequent request;
-- src:4459 | ( b )
-- src:4460 | to the admission as evidence in the proceedings of any opinion provided by the specified court pursuant to the initial request and any clarification provided by that court pursuant to any subsequent request; and
-- src:4461 | ( c )
-- src:4462 | to the dispensation with cross-examination of the maker of the opinion and clarification mentioned in sub-paragraph ( b ).
@ref O 29A r 2(1) (src:4457-4462)
GIVEN `the proceedings are before the Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a question relating to the law of a specified foreign country or to the application of such law arises` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all of the parties consent to the transmission of the initial request and any subsequent request` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all of the parties consent to the admission as evidence in the proceedings of any opinion and any clarification provided by the specified court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all of the parties consent to the dispensation with cross-examination of the maker of the opinion and clarification` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request is transmitted on the application of one or more of the parties or on the Court's own motion to a specified court in that specified foreign country` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 29A r 2(1) the Court may transmit a request for an opinion to a specified court` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings are before the Court` AND `a question relating to the law of a specified foreign country or to the application of such law arises` AND `all of the parties consent to the transmission of the initial request and any subsequent request` AND `all of the parties consent to the admission as evidence in the proceedings of any opinion and any clarification provided by the specified court` AND `all of the parties consent to the dispensation with cross-examination of the maker of the opinion and clarification`
    THEN IF `the request is transmitted on the application of one or more of the parties or on the Court's own motion to a specified court in that specified foreign country`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where in any proceedings before the Court there arises any question relating to the law of any specified foreign country or to the application of such law, the Court may, on the application of one or more of the parties or on the Court’s own motion, transmit to a specified court in that specified foreign country a request for an opinion on that question (called in this Rule the initial request), and any subsequent request for a clarification that is relevant to the opinion (called in this Rule a subsequent request), if all of the parties consent"
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where in any proceedings before the Court there arises any question relating to the law of any specified foreign country or to the application of such law, the Court may, on the application of one or more of the parties or on the Court’s own motion, transmit to a specified court in that specified foreign country a request for an opinion on that question (called in this Rule the initial request), and any subsequent request for a clarification that is relevant to the opinion (called in this Rule a subsequent request), if all of the parties consent"
